    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Design thinking, a deliberate process meant to foster creative and overall confidence, has been applied to numerous social issues. The method, however, has yet to be used to explore the lack of women in STEM (Science-Technology-Engineering-Math) fields, resulting from systemic sexism and lack of female confidence. This paper identifies design thinking as an implementable solution to increase women’s confidence as a way to help bridge the gender gap between men and women in STEM.",
